Theorem CN-6-Extraction-Reconciliation: ReturnContract pre-widening preserves CN-6 soundness

  Preconditions:
    - Annex E §AIMS.9 Return Provenance CN-6 notes describe STRUCTURAL
      EXTRACTION-TIME behavior
    - ReturnContract.uniqueness extractor traces structurally pre-widening
    - CN-6 fires on per-variable AimsState locality post-widening

  Soundness property:
    The ReturnContract Unique field reflects pre-widening structural state,
    NOT post-widening AimsState. Per-instruction extraction is sound vs
    CN-6 unconditional canonicalize on the separate per-variable lattice.

  Proof obligation:
    Finite enumeration over 8 return-instruction kinds (Construct, Reuse,
    CollectionReuse, PartialApply, ApplyWithContract, ApplyNoContract,
    Select, Project). For each, verify the extracted ReturnContract
    uniqueness value lies in the canonical Uniqueness carrier and reflects
    the per-instruction structural classification (not the post-widening
    per-variable AimsState).

    The two surfaces (AimsState vs ReturnContract) do not share storage;
    CN-6 canonicalize_single_pass cannot mutate ReturnContract.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (8-instruction-kind enumeration per
        section_03::verify_cn6_return_contract_extraction_reconciliation)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_03 case_analysis engine discharges CN-6-Extraction-Reconciliation via 8-kind return-instruction enumeration
